Step-by-Step Practical Demonstration
He proves how these concepts work in action using two separate browser logins (Root vs. Test User):

Step 1: Authentication without Authorization

He creates a new user (test-user-501) without attaching any policies.

He logs in as test-user-501. The login succeeds (Authentication works), but clicking on S3 or EC2 returns "Access Denied" errors (Authorization fails).

Step 2: Adding Authorization via Policies

He switches back to the Root account and attaches the AmazonS3FullAccess policy to test-user-501.

Switching back to test-user-501, the user can now successfully view and create S3 buckets.

Step 3: Scaling with User Groups

He creates a group called Development and attaches S3 and EC2 full access policies to the group.

Adding test-user-501 to the group automatically grants all group permissions at once, demonstrating how devops engineers manage permissions efficiently.
